  data: {
    LLM: "Memory is essential. When you flip a tile that doesn't match, memorize its pip values. When the line ends change later, you'll know if that specific tile can be played.\n\nOpponent Tracking: Watch what your opponents flip and return. If they return a 5-2, and you have control over the line ends, try to make one of the ends a 5 or 2 to force them to play a tile they might not want to.\n\nBlock Prevention: If you know your leftmost tile matches an end, but playing it would change that end to a value you know your *next* tile cannot match, consider the risk of blocking yourself.",
    Player: "Memory is essential. When you flip a tile that doesn't match, memorize its pip values. When the line ends change later, you'll know if that specific tile can be played.\n\nOpponent Tracking: Watch what your opponents flip and return. If they return a 5-2, and you have control over the line ends, try to make one of the ends a 5 or 2 to force them to play a tile they might not want to.\n\nBlock Prevention: If you know your leftmost tile matches an end, but playing it would change that end to a value you know your *next* tile cannot match, consider the risk of blocking yourself.",
